---
import '../styles/base.css';
import '../styles/signal-school.css';
const {title='signal-school'}=Astro.props;
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"/><meta name="description" content="A browser-only workspace for checking AI-assisted drafts against source notes."/><title>{title}</title></head><body><a href="#main" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a><noscript><main class="no-js-outline"><p class="signal-eyebrow">Signal School</p><h1>The Workroom needs JavaScript.</h1><p>You can still follow the route: state the request, keep the source notes with the draft, and record what another person should check before sharing it.</p><ol><li>Say what you need and who it is for.</li><li>Keep the relevant source notes with the draft.</li><li>Record what the notes establish, contradict, or leave open.</li></ol><p>Enable JavaScript to use the Workroom, guided lessons, and final challenge.</p></main></noscript><slot/><footer class="public-footer">Built by Saran Vashisht · Inputs stay in memory and clear on refresh.</footer></body></html>
